   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.2. Strengthened capacity of enterprises and their support systems to enhance productivity and sustainability</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Colabora Moda Sustent&#xE1;vel, a national innovation hub, was been strengthened. As part of the capacity building strategy approved by the CMS Governance Council in 2022, the ILO has provided Instituto REOS with technical support to foster best practices in circular economy and sustainability in the textile and garment value chain in Brazil: a) hybrid workshop on Regenerative and Circular Fashion; b) publication and dissemination of a Regenerative and Circular Fashion booklet; c) establishment of and support to two working groups, on Gender and Racial Equity in the fashion industry and on Training and Communication on regenerative fashion. Plus, in consultation with social partners ABIT, ABVTEX and the National Confederation of Industry (CNI), an implementation agreement has been signed with SENAI (National Service for Industrial Learning), the leading education, training and consultancy institution in Brazil, to increase its operational capacity in promoting the productivity of small and medium-sized firms of the garment sector in S&#xE3;o Paulo. The main results of the project during 2022 and 2023 have been: a) In partnership with the sector&apos;s social partners, the elaboration of a diagnosis on the main factors that affect the productivity of small and medium-sized companies in the clothing sector in the metropolitan region of S&#xE3;o Paulo; b) Based on the diagnosis, the elaboration of an implementation agreement (IA) with SENAI, to expand the institution&apos;s capacity to offer training focused on specific issues that affect the productivity of small and medium-sized companies in the garments in the metropolitan region of S&#xE3;o Paulo; c) as a result of the IA, training and certification of nine SENAI consultants in two SCORE modules from June 2023 to December 2023; d) as a result of this capacity building, SENAI has offered, two SCORE training modules to 14 firms in the textile sector, from June 2023 to October 2023, fostering within-firm productivity improvements. The ILO has actively contributed to the continuation of the activities of an important innovation hub in the garment value chain, Colabora Moda Sustent&#xE1;vel (CMS), by fostering the execution of workshops, a booklet and working groups to promote best practices in the topics of circular economy and sustainability in the textile and garment value chain in Brazil. 

The implementation agreement between the ILO and SENAI, in consultation with social partners ABIT and ABVTEX, is helping to increase the operational capacity of SENAI, a major Brazilian productivity institute. Nine of its consultants are being trained by the ILO in the SCORE methodology, starting June 2023. 

Through the agreement, two SCORE training modules have been offered to 14 firms in the textile sector, from June 2023 to October 2023, fostering within-firm productivity improvements, with the active participation of ILO staff and SCORE expert trainers and SENAI trainers.</narrative>
   </description>
